  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "18f59675-3920-3810-ab81-0e218f707e69",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "ee02e13a-6fb7-1263-e15b-aeb01542ce4f",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "At the certificate presentation ceremony, Dr Shamsh Kassim-Lakha, President of AKU, said \"It is most important that we deliver quality care to our patients and the ISO process will continue to be useful in ensuring compliance to the highest standards of care that we have set for ourselves\". ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"The ISO 9002 journey began in November 1997\", said Mr Nadeem Mustafa Khan, Chief Operating Officer of AKUH, \"and culminated with the final audit in February 1999. It was all hard work on the part of the staff. We were well-assisted by Mr 1mran Shariff of the Pakistan Institute of Quality Control (PIQC), who provided valuable on-going guidance\". ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Continued focus on providing care and services in accordance with the patient's needs is a must for AKUH\", informed Mr John B. Stevens, Director General of the Hospital. He further stressed that it is AKUH's intention to prepare the entire Hospital for an ISO 9002 certification in the year 2000.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
